---
import KickoffSession from "../../components/KickoffSession.astro";

const photos = [
    {
        src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5349.jpg",
        alt: "Alan Ho at the podium. The slide behind him is the civic welcome.",
        caption: "Opening the civic welcome.",
    },
    {
        src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5350.jpg",
        alt: "Francis Wang and Alan Ho hold a framed City of Markham proclamation.",
        caption: "With Francis Wang and the City of Markham proclamation.",
    },
    {
        src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5329.jpg",
        alt: "Alan Ho signs the Canada2080 kickoff banner.",
        caption: "Signing the kickoff banner.",
    },
    {
        src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5347.jpg",
        alt: "Alan Ho with speakers and guests holding the Canada2080 kickoff banner.",
        caption: "With speakers and guests, and the kickoff banner.",
    },
    {
        src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5343.jpg",
        alt: "The kickoff group, including Alan Ho, holding the signed banner.",
        caption: "The room, with the banner.",
    },
];
---

<KickoffSession
    documentTitle="The future is not guaranteed. It is made. | Canada2080"
    description="Alan Ho's civic welcome at the Canada2080 kickoff. The future is not guaranteed. It is made."
    eyebrow="Civic welcome · 1:05 p.m."
    headline="The future is not guaranteed."
    claim="It is made."
    name="Alan Ho"
    bio="Alan Ho is York Regional Councillor for the City of Markham and Chair of Markham's Culture and Economic Development Committee."
    profileUrl="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alan-ho-976aa03b/"
    podiumSrc="/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5349.jpg"
    podiumAlt="Alan Ho at the podium. The slide behind him is the civic welcome."
    photos={photos}
>
    <p class="lede">
        Abundance has to be shared. Resilience has to be built on purpose. Both
        depend on the choices made now.
    </p>
    <p>
        Alan Ho opened the Canada2080 kickoff with a welcome about 2080: a
        future of abundance and resilience. Soaring technology, cleaner energy,
        longer lives, and thriving communities are a picture. They are not a
        promise.
    </p>
    <p>The work, as he set it out, starts in four places.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Protect water, parks, and climate.</li>
        <li>Plan housing and transit for every generation.</li>
        <li>Take up innovation, and still safeguard dignity.</li>
        <li>Strengthen local food, health, and social connection.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Resilience, in his definition, is more than surviving a shock. It is
        adapting, recovering, and growing together. Abundance is more than
        having more. It is enough opportunity, and enough hope, for everyone.
    </p>
    <p>
        He pictured Markham, and places beyond it, where seniors are supported,
        young people can afford to stay, newcomers belong, and neighbourhoods
        stay green and safe. That takes courage, collaboration, and a longer
        view than the next political cycle.
    </p>
    <p class="close-line">Imagine boldly. Plan wisely. Act together.</p>
    <Fragment slot="transcript">
        <p class="transcript-note">Cleaned up transcripts.</p>
        <blockquote>
            <p>
                Well, good afternoon everyone, and welcome. My name is Alan Ho,
                York Regional Councillor for the City of Markham. I'm also the
                Chair of Markham's Culture and Economic Development Committee.
                It is my great, great pleasure to be here today with you all,
                and today it is an honour to open this important conversation
                about 2080: a future of abundance and resilience.
            </p>
            <p>
                When we imagine 2080, we may picture soaring technology,
                cleaner energy, longer lives, and thriving communities. That
                future is not guaranteed. Abundance must be shared and
                resilience must be built deliberately.
            </p>
            <p>
                It begins with choices we make today: protecting our water,
                parks, and climate; planning housing and transit for all
                generations; embracing innovation while safeguarding dignity;
                and strengthening local food, health, and social connection.
            </p>
            <p>
                Resilience is not only surviving shocks. It is adapting,
                recovering, and growing together. Abundance is not only having
                more. It is ensuring everyone has enough opportunity and hope.
            </p>
            <p>
                In the City of Markham and beyond, we can create a future where
                seniors are supported, young people can afford to stay,
                newcomers belong, and neighbourhoods are green and safe.
            </p>
            <p>
                That future demands courage, collaboration, and long-term
                thinking. So let us move beyond short-term politics and build
                lasting prosperity. Let us imagine boldly, plan wisely, and act
                together.
            </p>
            <p>
                Thank you for being part of this journey towards 2080: a future
                of abundance and resilience for all. Thank you very much.
            </p>
        </blockquote>
    </Fragment>
</KickoffSession>
